---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, whoWeAre } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="About" description="What the Osaka Indian Association is and who it is for.">
  <section class="band head">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <h1>About Us</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A vibrant community connecting Indian students, researchers, professionals, alumni, and prospective students across Osaka.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band top">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <p>
        The Osaka Indian Association is a community that brings together Indian students, researchers, professionals, and alumni living in and around Osaka. 
        We aim to foster meaningful connections, support newcomers, celebrate Indian culture, and provide a welcoming community for Indians at every stage of their journey in Japan.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whether you are a current student looking to connect with other Indians, a researcher or professional building your network in Osaka, or a prospective student preparing 
        to come to Japan, the association is a place to connect, learn, and participate.
      </p>

      <!-- <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <dl class="groups">
        {
          whoWeAre.map((g) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{g.group}</dt>
              <dd>{g.note}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl> -->

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>
        We organise events and activities throughout the year that bring the community together. These include cultural celebrations, social gatherings, sports activities, and 
        opportunities to meet other members of the Indian community.
      </p>
      <p>
        Beyond events, we aim to make it easier for people to settle into life in Osaka. Members share practical experiences and information about university life, housing, local 
        procedures, daily life in Japan, and other matters that can be particularly useful for newcomers and prospective students.
      </p>

      <h2>For current and prospective students</h2>
      <p>
        For current students, the association provides an opportunity to meet people from different universities, academic fields, and professional backgrounds, while staying 
        connected with the wider Indian community.
      </p>
      <p>
        For prospective students and those preparing to move to Osaka, the community can be a useful starting point for learning about life in Japan, understanding the student 
        experience, and connecting with people who have already made the transition.
      </p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        The association is run by volunteers from within the community. There is no membership fee, and participation in the community does not require a formal application.
      </p>
      <p>
        Events and activities may have associated costs, such as venue or catering expenses. Whenever applicable, these costs are communicated in advance.
      </p>

      <h2>Get involved</h2>
      <p>
        The association grows through the participation and contributions of its members. Whether you would like to help organise an event, contribute your skills, share 
        useful information with newcomers, or simply meet other members of the community, we welcome your participation.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn" href={site.joinFormUrl || '/contact/'}>Get in touch</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) 0;
  }

  .top {
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 2.8rem;
  }

  .groups {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }

  .groups div {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--marigold);
  }

  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    color: var(--indigo);
  }
</style>
